{"duration_api_ms":88508,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"59f7e954-9bfb-4dc9-8631-d80527346979","total_cost_usd":0.6797998,"usage":{"input_tokens":24,"cache_creation_input_tokens":52528,"cache_read_input_tokens":420499,"output_tokens":8769,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1270},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":52528,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":873,"cache_read_input_tokens":54205,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4303,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4303},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":24,"outputTokens":8769,"cacheReadInputTokens":420499,"cacheCreationInputTokens":52528,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.6797998,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":1270,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":14,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I wrote the plan for CAT-02 to `tasks/CAT-02/plan.md`. The story is `status: adopted`, meaning the product page already exists, so the plan changes no production code and no existing test. For each of the five scenarios it records where the behaviour lives and which test covers it. It opens no `needs-human` question.\n\n**Context:** the story belongs to the `product` context. The designed and generated context maps agree on it, and the story's criteria name the product page themselves, so no new page or endpoint was needed.\n\n**Where the behaviour lives:**\n- **Route:** `ProductPageController.java:86-101` serves the product page.\n- **Content:** `detail.pug` has the breadcrumb (lines 4-9), heading (13), image (20-22), description (31-33), \"Category\" (35-38) and the \"Back to Products\" link (54).\n- **Tab title:** the view model sets it to the product name (`ProductDetailPageViewModel.java:66`) and `layout.pug:7` renders it.\n- **Entry point:** the card's \"View Details\" link is at `catalog.pug:30`.\n- **Seed data:** the seeded products the scenarios name are in `SampleDataInitializer.java`.\n\n**Test levels:** the happy path (`view-details-opens-the-product-page`) is planned as a Playwright end-to-end test. The other four scenarios are planned as integration tests.\n\n**Test coverage:** no scenario has a test that checks it as the story states it.\n- `ProductCatalogPageIntegrationTest.everyCardOffersAViewDetailsLinkToThatProductsPage` partly covers the happy path: it follows each card's link and checks that the page contains the product name, but not that the heading reads it. That file is uncommitted CAT-01 work.\n- Existing end-to-end tests open a product page, but always the first product (\"Bounded Context\" Enamel Pin), and none checks its contents.\n- A page-object method for going back to the catalogue, `ProductDetailPage.backToCatalog`, exists but no test calls it.\n\n**Open assumptions in the plan:** the heading, image, description, category and title have no `data-test` attributes, which the product description asks for on anything a test addresses. The plan notes this for a later stage and doesn't change the markup.\n\nI didn't run the story gate or any later stage.","ttft_ms":4881,"type":"result","duration_ms":89196,"uuid":"2e1c7f9a-a44a-45eb-995b-a22ffb29f400","ttft_stream_ms":3934,"time_to_request_ms":32,"first_content_frame_ms":3934,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_i